  "limits": [
    "No authentication. `who` is whatever the caller says it is, so the acknowledgement trail records a claim rather than an identity.",
    "Polling, not push. The page re-fetches; nothing is streamed, and an asset that degrades between polls is seen at the next one.",
    "Re-arming is evaluated on READ. A service nobody opens does not re-arm anything -- which is the safe direction (nothing is silenced by a service that is not running) and does mean an expired acknowledgement is not noticed until somebody looks.",
    "No notification. Re-arming changes what the screen shows and tells nobody.",
    "One process, one SQLite file. It is a shop-floor screen, not a fleet platform."
